Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.00,0:03:16.02,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,900,3350,3900)\pos(640,551.733)}Battles in the North and South
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.44,0:03:22.72,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,900,4500,5210)\pos(653.755,434.522)}Episode 67\N\N\N\N\NSeven Capturings of Meng Huo
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.66,0:03:43.20,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Following the fifth capture and release\Nof Meng Huo,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.21,0:03:48.42,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang took the city of Sanjiang and closed in on Yinkeng Hill.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.60,0:03:52.47,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Seeing this situation,\NLady Zhurong, wife of Meng Huo,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.52,0:03:57.11,Thinking,,0,0,0,,came personally to battle the Shu troops in front of the hill.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.46,0:03:55.75,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(318.667,508)}Lady Zhùróng
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.34,0:04:00.56,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Let me capture her!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.56,0:04:02.56,Default,,0,0,0,,On guard!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.71,0:04:05.62,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Don't run!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.28,0:04:17.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Charge!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.78,0:04:22.15,Default,,0,0,0,,General Zhang, look out!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.92,0:04:25.02,Default,,0,0,0,,General Zhang!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.30,0:04:45.78,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(978.667,576)}Mèng Huò
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.72,0:05:07.10,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(326.667,458.667)}Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: \NKǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.05,0:05:07.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I did not expect people like this in the South.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.90,0:05:10.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, let me lead the attack tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.42,0:05:15.78,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(277.918,506.787)}Zhào Yún\NStyled: Zǐlóng
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.06,0:05:13.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I will cut down Lady Zhurong for certain,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.92,0:05:15.74,Default,,0,0,0,,and puncture that Meng Huo's ego.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.16,0:05:16.67,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.05,0:05:21.22,Default,,0,0,0,,General Zhang and Ma are still within captivity.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.28,0:05:26.72,Default,,0,0,0,,We need a plan to capture her alive tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.91,0:05:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not harm Lady Zhurong in any way.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.50,0:05:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise, Meng Huo would be hell bent on fighting us.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.12,0:05:37.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Come.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.51,0:05:40.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, you will...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.38,0:05:48.35,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(312,512)}Wèi Yán\NStyled: Wéncháng
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.64,0:06:03.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you running!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.22,0:06:06.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You've come again to court death!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.31,0:06:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.51,0:06:19.39,Default,,0,0,0,,On guard!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.84,0:06:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Coward, where are you running?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.62,0:07:08.15,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(297.333,220)}Mǎ Dài
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.51,0:07:07.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you running?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.62,0:07:09.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you running!?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.28,0:07:22.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Untie her at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.24,0:07:27.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Lady Zhurong, my apologies.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.24,0:07:34.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Let her rest, and prepare wine and food for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.48,0:07:36.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.12,0:07:42.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam, I've sent someone to notify Meng Huo.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.12,0:07:45.92,Default,,0,0,0,,You can return home soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.60,0:07:50.06,Default,,0,0,0,,In exchange, please return our two officers.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.51,0:08:02.31,Default,,0,0,0,,My lady!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.28,0:08:06.61,Default,,0,0,0,,-Open the gate! \N-Aye!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.04,0:08:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,My lady!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.62,0:08:21.24,Default,,0,0,0,,My lady!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.52,0:08:24.34,Default,,0,0,0,,My lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.32,0:08:28.10,Default,,0,0,0,,My beloved.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.24,0:08:40.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Rest assured, the King of Pana Ravine is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.68,0:08:43.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, we'll fight the Shu men and avenge your honor!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.68,0:09:00.42,Default,,0,0,0,,We've been waiting for quite some time, where are they?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.32,0:09:04.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it a trick of the Southerners?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.40,0:09:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,We've waited long enough. Shall we go back?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.08,0:09:14.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us fall back.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.64,0:09:19.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Back to the camp!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.64,0:09:42.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Formations!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.79,0:09:54.95,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(341.334,516.333)}King Mùlù
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.86,0:10:17.22,Default,,0,0,0,,In all my years of fighting, \NI've never seen formations such as this!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.80,0:10:30.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Ready archers!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.58,0:10:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Archers, ready!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.76,0:10:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Shoot!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.60,0:11:03.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.97,0:11:04.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.60,0:11:27.92,Default,,0,0,0,,We have failed our mission, Chancellor. We deserve reprimand.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.93,0:11:29.14,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not your fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.52,0:11:35.14,Default,,0,0,0,,When I was in Longzhong, I heard of \Nthe Southerners' skill at taming wild animals.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.90,0:11:39.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Thus, I made special preparations for this expedition.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.22,0:11:43.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, I shall engage the enemy personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.82,0:11:44.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.89,0:12:04.36,Default,,0,0,0,,That is Zhuge Liang in that chariot!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.04,0:12:08.70,Default,,0,0,0,,If we can capture him, victory will be ours!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.68,0:12:13.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Rest easy, my king. He'll be no harder to capture than a lost sheep!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.06,0:12:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.96,0:12:20.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, do be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.84,0:12:38.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Beloved, this time we will avenge the shame of my five captures.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.32,0:12:47.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.98,0:13:40.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat! Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.38,0:13:44.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Order all troops, after them!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.24,0:14:24.22,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(986.667,510.667)}Dàilái \NDòngzhǔ \N(Chief of \NDàilái Ravine)
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.90,0:14:36.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Our stronghold is in the hands of the enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.12,0:14:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Where can we go now?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.42,0:14:44.90,Default,,0,0,0,,My king, we can go to King of Wuge for shelter.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.10,0:14:46.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sure he won't stand by.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.92,0:14:50.12,Default,,0,0,0,,We've already visited several chieftains.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.36,0:14:53.12,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(878.667,573.333)}Mèng Yōu
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.30,0:14:52.02,Default,,0,0,0,,None of it worked out.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.68,0:14:55.24,Default,,0,0,0,,How can we bear to face anyone else now?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.96,0:14:59.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It seems that we're no match for Zhuge Liang.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.47,0:15:01.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.08,0:15:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,now that it's come to this, \Nwe should just yield to the Shu men.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.00,0:15:05.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Nonsense!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.90,0:15:11.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I will not rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.54,0:15:14.88,Default,,0,0,0,,It's now or nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.60,0:15:17.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd rather die than surrender!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.98,0:15:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,My king, do not worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.82,0:15:24.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a plan, if you like?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.46,0:15:25.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Say it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.98,0:16:05.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Set all the captives free. \NLet them go back to their homes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.25,0:16:05.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.71,0:16:11.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, Chief of Dailai Ravine, brother-in-law of Meng Huo,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.60,0:16:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,tried to persuade Meng Huo to surrender, but failed.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.18,0:16:18.14,Default,,0,0,0,,He has taken him, his wife, and hundreds of his clan as prisoners.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.15,0:16:19.56,Default,,0,0,0,,He has brought them to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.56,0:16:20.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are they now?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.97,0:16:22.30,Default,,0,0,0,,They're at the foot of the hill.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.56,0:16:25.50,Default,,0,0,0,,-Let them wait outside the ravine. \N{\i1}-Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.02,0:16:29.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You two officers.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.86,0:16:32.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Present!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.80,0:16:42.64,Default,,0,0,0,,The Chief of Dailai Ravine may enter.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.00,0:16:58.60,Default,,0,0,0,,No soldiers are admitted.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.47,0:17:02.68,Default,,0,0,0,,King and Lady, if you please.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.28,0:17:17.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Come here, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.82,0:17:30.32,Default,,0,0,0,,My respects to Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.44,0:17:36.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Tie him!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.00,0:17:40.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, but I've brought Meng Huo and his whole family here-!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.68,0:17:48.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.22,0:17:58.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.96,0:18:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Hiding daggers on your person.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.92,0:18:07.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Obviously an attempt to assassinate me. \NWhat do you say to that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.56,0:18:09.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Vile Zhuge Liang!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.38,0:18:11.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Just kill me, why waste your breath!?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.02,0:18:18.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Last time you were captured, you said you would yield only when I captured you at your home.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.80,0:18:20.66,Default,,0,0,0,,What else can you say now?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.46,0:18:26.51,Default,,0,0,0,,We came here of our own volition,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.51,0:18:29.04,Default,,0,0,0,,not because of you, I will not yield!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.05,0:18:29.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Meng Huo!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.68,0:18:33.76,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the sixth time I've captured you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.90,0:18:36.18,Default,,0,0,0,,How could you go back on your word now?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.26,0:18:38.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}This is not because of my dishonesty,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.18,0:18:40.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}but because of your unjust masters!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.06,0:18:45.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}How is our master unjust?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.82,0:18:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The two Riverlands belonged to the tribesmen, \Nand your masters stole it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.18,0:18:53.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}Now you cravenly intrude into the South.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.61,0:18:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}We've lived on this land for generations,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.40,0:18:58.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}how can I give it all to others?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.53,0:19:01.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}Sheer nonsense, words of a hypocrite!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.60,0:19:07.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Only those who have the hearts and favor of the people can inherit the land.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.55,0:19:11.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}When the realm was in chaos, and people left to suffer,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.19,0:19:15.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}it was the late emperor that brought peace to the land of Shu, and let its people prosper.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.48,0:19:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Yet all you've done in meantime is wage war, killing our officials,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.02,0:19:22.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\}intruded upon our borders \Nand terrorized the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.62,0:19:24.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}Since we marched southward,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.28,0:19:27.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}you've gone back on your word time \Nand again, raising only arms against us.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.83,0:19:32.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}You have brought devastation on the land, \Nand plunged your own people into great misery.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.92,0:19:36.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}Your crimes anger the people and even the Heavens!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.40,0:19:39.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}If you still refuse to yield,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.34,0:19:43.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}how could you face your elders and brothers of the South?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.93,0:19:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.30,0:20:00.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I, Meng Huo, have one last \Nplan to overcome the Shu army.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.81,0:20:04.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14)}If I still refuse to yield, you may kill me and my whole family!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.64,0:20:15.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.38,0:20:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,-Very well. \N-Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.90,0:20:24.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Since you still refuse to yield, \NI will release you one last time.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.98,0:20:33.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I will endure the flames of war raging across this land.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.90,0:20:38.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Let those wounded soldiers raise their swords and spears once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.94,0:20:42.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}You alone will bear these sins!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.94,0:20:47.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665)}Untie him.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.70,0:20:53.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Release them all.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.40,0:21:01.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor, for your mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.48,0:21:02.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.36,0:21:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.42,0:21:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, we'll meet again.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.46,0:21:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.68,0:21:35.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, Meng Huo has called on the Chief of the Wuge, leading 30,000 rattan armored troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.08,0:21:37.98,Default,,0,0,0,,They're challenging us at the ferry crossing of Taohua River.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.85,0:21:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Onwards to Taohua.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.34,0:21:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.67,0:22:04.69,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(748,570.667)}Wùtūgǔ
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.84,0:22:08.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Charge!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.34,0:22:29.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Charge!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.64,0:22:34.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Loose!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.06,0:22:42.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Shoot!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.36,0:22:46.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Shoot!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:42.26,0:24:43.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.28,0:24:48.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}It's said that this armor is made of rattan, grown in the gullies.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:48.76,0:24:53.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The cut rattan is soaked in oil \Nfor half a year, then dried in the sunlight.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.90,0:24:57.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}After drying, they are soaked in oil again, and the process is repeated many times.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.16,0:25:00.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665.670)}Then they are made into armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.60,0:25:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}With this armor on, \Nthe men can float across the river,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.10,0:25:08.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}never getting wet in water, \Nand no sword can penetrate it.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.94,0:25:14.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Meng Huo with his rattan-armored army is a great threat.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.64,0:25:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665.670)}It will be difficult to overcome him now.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.12,0:25:24.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, I have a plan to crush them utterly, leaving none standing.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.06,0:25:26.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Then tell us.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.04,0:25:30.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Fire attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.35,0:25:31.51,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(342.667,500)}Jiǎng Wǎn\NStyled: Gōngyǎn
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.52,0:25:35.85,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right, fire! Fire, Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.88,0:25:51.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What is the name of this valley?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.95,0:25:55.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, it is called the "Winding Serpent Valley."
Dialogue: 0,0:25:56.14,0:25:58.48,Default,,0,0,0,,At the other end, it leads to Sanjiang.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.82,0:26:05.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Chancellor, our army is exhausted from the expedition.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.78,0:26:07.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665.670)}We cannot fight the Southern army for long.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.91,0:26:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665.670)}Furthermore, winter is approaching,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.00,0:26:12.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14)}and our men's clothes are too light to keep them warm.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:12.88,0:26:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid that-
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.84,0:26:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Chancellor, I'm afraid we can't be here through winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.70,0:27:04.63,Default,,0,0,0,,General Ma.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:05.00,0:27:05.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.52,0:27:10.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I now give you ten tanks of black oil and a thousand bamboo poles.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:10.72,0:27:15.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, you are to keep the two ends of the valley with your men.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:17.00,0:27:21.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything must be ready within half a month.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.16,0:27:27.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyone who leaks these orders will be punished under military law.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:27.71,0:27:28.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.76,0:27:42.24,Default,,0,0,0,,-Zilong. \N-Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:44.87,0:27:46.31,Default,,0,0,0,,When you enter the valley,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.40,0:27:54.24,Default,,0,0,0,,prepare wagons of straw and timber, as soon as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.64,0:27:58.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, guard the road that leads to Sanjiang.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.42,0:28:00.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.96,0:28:06.13,Default,,0,0,0,,-Wenchang.\N-Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:06.77,0:28:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Encamp your detachment at the ferry crossing of Taohua River.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.20,0:28:15.89,Default,,0,0,0,,If the Southern army comes over the river, you are to abandon camp and march deep into the valley.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.16,0:28:20.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Within half a month, you need to be defeated fifteen times.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.06,0:28:22.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Abandon a total of seven camps.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.80,0:28:23.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, I-
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.30,0:28:27.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Not one defeat less. Or else, do not come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:28.80,0:28:29.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.50,0:29:05.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Report! The Shu men have fled into the valley, shall we pursue them?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.06,0:29:12.08,Default,,0,0,0,,These are barren hills, nothing grows here. Pursue them!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.36,0:29:37.32,Default,,0,0,0,,What is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.65,0:29:40.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief, this valley must be the supply line of the Shu army.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:40.46,0:29:43.14,Default,,0,0,0,,They likely abandoned their grain carts.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.14,0:29:45.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Make haste! After them!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.15,0:31:07.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.28,0:31:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.60,0:31:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.18,0:31:20.45,Default,,0,0,0,,-Take her! \N{\i1}-Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.65,0:31:27.92,Default,,0,0,0,,-Chancellor!\N-Well done, General Wei! Well done!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.00,0:31:40.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, you...?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:43.44,0:31:47.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}The Southern men were obstinate, \Nthere was no other choice but to use fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:51.72,0:31:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665.670)}This plan could only be done as a last resort.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.52,0:32:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Such a senseless, cruel massacre. \NMy conscience will not be at ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:05.64,0:32:08.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665.670)}I've fulfilled my duty for the sake of our nation,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:08.96,0:32:11.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665.670)}yet my life will be shortened in return.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:17.38,0:32:20.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665.670)}Leave one side open. If there are still survivors,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.46,0:32:23.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,665.670)}let them escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.94,0:32:27.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:11.44,0:33:16.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, our fallen comrades shall be avenged!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:17.24,0:33:18.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Execute them!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.74,0:33:21.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Get in!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.16,0:33:29.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.10,0:33:30.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.40,0:33:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,General Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:33.18,0:33:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor's orders,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.18,0:33:38.18,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(964.347,467.334)}Mǎ Sù\NStyled: Yòucháng
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.51,0:33:37.36,Default,,0,0,0,,do not harm the Southern King, let him go.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:41.57,0:33:42.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Untie him.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:43.04,0:33:43.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.08,0:33:49.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, sir! Thank you for your mercy!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.26,0:33:51.52,Default,,0,0,0,,It was Chancellor who let you go. Thank him.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:52.50,0:33:54.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank the Chancellor for his mercy!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:54.74,0:33:57.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Please rise. Untie them!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:57.46,0:33:57.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:59.23,0:34:00.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.68,0:34:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, Lady Zhurong is waiting for you at the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:08.16,0:34:08.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.05,0:34:12.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.26,0:34:24.24,Default,,0,0,0,,My king!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.10,0:34:28.90,Default,,0,0,0,,My king, my king!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:39.52,0:34:42.28,Default,,0,0,0,,My king, do we still fight?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:42.50,0:34:49.43,Default,,0,0,0,,My king, please have pity on us, no more wars! No more!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:49.43,0:34:51.17,Default,,0,0,0,,No more!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:18.77,0:35:21.74,Default,,0,0,0,,My king!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:26.52,0:35:27.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Beloved!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.68,0:35:31.42,Default,,0,0,0,,My king.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.59,0:35:42.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My king!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.51,0:35:48.23,Default,,0,0,0,,My king.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.54,0:35:53.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:56.98,0:35:59.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.05,0:36:04.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor thought Your Highness would have a long journey ahead,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:04.46,0:36:10.34,Default,,0,0,0,,so he asked me to bring you some food and clean water for you on your journey.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:54.86,0:36:55.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Beloved.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:57.44,0:37:00.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Go back, go to the Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:14.98,0:37:19.12,Thinking,,0,0,0,,On the first day of September of the third year of the Jianxing era (225 CE),
Dialogue: 0,0:37:19.88,0:37:23.46,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang led the army towards the Lu River.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:26.40,0:37:30.72,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Suddenly, the clouds turned dark, and the wind raged on.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:31.28,0:37:35.23,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Waves of the river grew strong, \Nand the army could move no further.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:40.14,0:37:45.10,Thinking,,0,0,0,,According to the local people, this was due to the wrathful spirits of the recent dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.18,0:37:58.64,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Thus, Zhuge Liang followed their rules of ceremony, and ordered sacrifice of oxen and horse,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.64,0:38:04.12,Thinking,,0,0,0,,with dough molded in the shape of human heads.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.54,0:38:08.42,Thinking,,0,0,0,,The dough, stuffed with the meat of oxen and lamb, was named "mántou,"
Dialogue: 0,0:38:08.42,0:38:18.40,Thinking,,0,0,0,,and was offered as sacrifice at the altar built to \Nthe River Lu, to appease the spirits of the dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:37.68,0:39:42.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I, Zhuge Liang, under His Majesty's blessing, led this expedition into the south.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:42.68,0:39:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,680)}Through our many battles,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:44.82,0:39:51.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}we are grateful for the assistance and grace given to us by the people of the South.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:52.86,0:39:56.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,680)}Now, King Meng Huo has returned to the light,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:56.48,0:40:00.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}giving up arms in the name of benevolence and greater good for the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:00.53,0:40:02.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,680)}By this, I am moved greatly.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.16,0:40:05.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:08.74,0:40:12.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Meng Huo thanks the Chancellor for your kindness.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:12.86,0:40:14.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Rise up, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:17.38,0:40:24.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, I present the Chancellor all the lands of the South, its people, armies and cattle.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:28.46,0:40:33.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor's Heavenly might will never be met with opposition.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:40.36,0:40:44.72,Default,,0,0,0,,This Chancellor now returns all ownership of the South back to Meng Huo.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.58,0:40:50.41,Default,,0,0,0,,May you live on as King of the South.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:50.74,0:40:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,All matters of Nanzhong will remain yours to be cared for.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:55.76,0:40:59.12,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Chancellor, I am but a guilty man!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:59.54,0:41:02.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Sparing my life is a mercy I cannot repay.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:02.62,0:41:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,How can I still remain as King?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:06.52,0:41:08.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Please appoint someone else, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:11.40,0:41:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I've captured and released you seven times, all due to my trust in Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:15.43,0:41:17.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Why should this be given to someone else?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:19.36,0:41:22.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I only wish for Your Highness to not betray the trust of His Majesty,
Dialogue: 0,0:41:22.82,0:41:24.64,Default,,0,0,0,,and the will of the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:42.32,0:41:46.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I, Meng Huo, will do my all to care for the land of Nanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:46.74,0:41:49.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise, may I be punished by Heaven and Earth!
Dialogue: 0,0:41:57.56,0:41:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:41:59.06,0:42:00.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:42:00.32,0:42:01.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.62,0:42:04.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Please rise.

